A dedicated RAG filter chip is positioned at the extreme right of the filter bar. When one or more RAG filters are applied, they are represented within this chip. If no RAG filters are applied, this space remains empty.



The filter side drawer contains all available filter options, including both table filters and RAG filters. If the number of filter options exceeds the available viewport height, the filter section becomes scrollable.

The footer actions remain sticky and always visible, regardless of the scroll position. The footer includes:

• Apply — Applies the selected filters and updates the results.

• Cancel — Closes the side drawer without applying any changes made during the current session.

• Reset — Clears all applied filters and restores the default filter state. The reset action is applied only after the user selects Apply.
